{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545586-glanced-through-laws-of-the-night-gehenna-war","id":1545586,"title":"Glanced through Laws of the Night/Gehenna War","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-08T15:01:40-08:00","id":1545586,"title":"Glanced through Laws of the Night/Gehenna War","content":"My initial impression is that with Laws of the Night is that covers old ground from the previous sourcebooks with some new predator types and clan archtypes and now we can play members of the 9th generation as long there from the ranks of the ancillae and a mention that we can play that generation as the Beckoning is not as strong as it is for the more potent generations.<br /> <br /> Personally I think that they should've kept them out of player creation rules and I wonder in how much time will pass before the 8th generation will be available.<br /> <br /> I'll probably pick it up later and get a more through reading.<br /> <br /> Gehenna War at first glance seems to be the better of the two books as it covers how widespread the conflict is and how the factions are enduring it and a list of 7 active ancients and cliff notes of there backstory and rumors of what they are planning and at least we have three new lore sheets to choose from.<br /> <br /> On a side note it seems now that Agata Starek is not a member of the Ventrue clan and is a member of the Brujah, I don't know if this is a typo or a retcon but then we weren't using her in our game anyway.<br /> <br /> So what are your thoughts on the two books?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-08T15:09:16-08:00","id":1545588,"title":"","content":"I don't recall seeing Agata being given a specific clan in <i>Anarch</i>. I think the &quot;Ventrue Ancilla&quot; mentioned on her Loresheet is the one who is scared of her, not her. It isn't the clearest writing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-08T17:38:52-08:00","id":1545591,"title":"","content":"On closer inspection. Maybe making the 9th generation kindred available had to happen because on page 215 or 220 on the main Vampire The Masquerade corebook we had the guidelines for Blood Potency of 5 rating. We know that the 10th-11th generations max at 4, but that could be fixed by adjusting the max to 5 for these two generations and keep the 9th generation out of play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-08T17:40:33-08:00","id":1545592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>higgipedia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545586-glanced-through-laws-of-the-night-gehenna-war?p=1545588#post1545588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recall seeing Agata being given a specific clan in <i>Anarch</i>. I think the &quot;Ventrue Ancilla&quot; mentioned on her Loresheet is the one who is scared of her, not her. It isn't the clearest writing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll have to reread the description for her, but I was given the strong impression that Agata Starek was a member of the Blue Bloods and she scared the clan because she didn't act like them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-08T19:10:32-08:00","id":1545596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1545586-glanced-through-laws-of-the-night-gehenna-war#post1545586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial impression is that with Laws of the Night is that covers old ground from the previous sourcebooks with some new predator types and clan archtypes and now we can play members of the 9th generation as long there from the ranks of the ancillae and a mention that we can play that generation as the Beckoning is not as strong as it is for the more potent generations.<br /> <br /> Personally I think that they should've kept them out of player creation rules and I wonder in how much time will pass before the 8th generation will be available.<br /> <br /> I'll probably pick it up later and get a more through reading.<br /> <br /> Gehenna War at first glance seems to be the better of the two books as it covers how widespread the conflict is and how the factions are enduring it and a list of 7 active ancients and cliff notes of there backstory and rumors of what they are planning and at least we have three new lore sheets to choose from.<br /> <br /> On a side note it seems now that Agata Starek is not a member of the Ventrue clan and is a member of the Brujah, I don't know if this is a typo or a retcon but then we weren't using her in our game anyway.<br /> <br /> So what are your thoughts on the two books?</div> </div> </div> </div>In Memoriam being released next year allows you to play ancilla characters and I think extends playable Generations to 8th.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-08T20:40:10-08:00","id":1545601,"title":"","content":"I guess it could work if they keep the lower generations like 8th or 9th in the ancillae range, but this is a huge departure from the start of the restored line.<br /> <br /> Still in our game it would work as we chose to have the most visible power players of the society would be members of 7th-11th generations and that the 4th-6th generation are becoming increasingly reclusive and work through proxies. It's a big change from the earlier material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 11-08-2024, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-12T18:41:18-08:00","id":1545762,"title":"","content":"Does Gehenna War add anything to action mechanics that might be useful to W5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"ht